  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Monique. You're verified, and I've checked the delivery records for your four recent orders. I've added **$30.00 in account credit**, and your balance is now $30.00. Here's what I found for each order:\n\n**Credited:**\n- **Saffron Lane (K-6501, today):** Promised by 6:00 PM, delivered at 6:52 PM, so 52 minutes late. For deliveries 45 or more minutes late, we credit 20% of the subtotal, up to $25 for Plus members. 20% of $128.00 would be $25.60, so you got the $25.00 maximum.\n- **Pho Real (K-6502, Oct 22):** Promised by 7:15 PM, delivered at 7:45 PM, so 30 minutes late. Plus orders have no delivery fee, so the credit for 16\u201344 minutes late is **$5.00**.\n\n**Not eligible:**\n- **Taqueria Luz (K-6503, Oct 20):** At 5:50 PM we sent you a push notification changing the estimated time to 7:00 PM. Because that came more than 30 minutes before the original time, 7:00 PM became the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, only 12 minutes after that. An order counts as late when it's more than 15 minutes past the promised time, so this one doesn't qualify.\n- **Burger Barn (K-6504, Oct 16):** This order was an hour late. However, late compensation has to be requested within 7 days of delivery, and that window closed yesterday at 8:00 PM. I'm sorry, but I can't credit it.\n\nLate deliveries are always compensated with account credit rather than a refund to your card. The credit will be applied automatically to your next order. Do these match your notes, or is there an order I haven't covered?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The amounts for Saffron Lane and Pho Real match my notes, so thanks for that. Why don't Taqueria Luz and Burger Barn count? I didn't get a notification about Taqueria changing the time, so I'm not sure how that works."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why that's frustrating. Here's how each one works.\n\n**Taqueria Luz (K-6503)**\nOur delivery records are what we go by for delivery timing. For this order, they show that at 5:50 PM we updated the estimated delivery time from 6:30 PM to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. The records also show that a push notification about the change went to you. Our rule is that if a new time is sent to you at least 30 minutes before the original promised time, the new time becomes the promised time. This update came 40 minutes early, so the promised time became 7:00 PM. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, which is within the 15-minute grace period.\n\nIt's possible the notification didn't show up on your phone. For example, push notifications might be turned off for Forkful, or your phone may have grouped it with other alerts. You can check your notification settings to make sure you see updates like this in future. Still, our records show it was sent, so I can't treat this order as late.\n\n**Burger Barn (K-6504)**\nThis order was an hour late, and normally that would qualify for credit. But you have to request late-delivery credit within 7 days of the delivery. The order arrived October 16 at 8:00 PM, so the window closed yesterday, October 23, at 8:00 PM. That's a firm limit, so I'm not able to credit it now. I'm sorry this one missed the cutoff by less than a day.\n\nThe $30.00 credit for Saffron Lane and Pho Real is already in your account. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I understand the Taqueria explanation, though I never got that notification, so I'll check my settings. I accept that Burger Barn is past the window. Before we finish, there's one more problem. Thursday's Pho Real order (#6502) was also missing the summer rolls, and I'd like those compensated with account credit."
  },
